AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) is playing an increasingly prominent ole in medicine because of advances in computing power, learning lgorithms, and the availability of large datasets (big data) sourced rom medical records and wearable health monitors. Disruptions n healthcare resulting from the COVID-19 pandemic have only furher encouraged the integration of AI into a variety of medical subelds. While AI is being used in other medical specializations such s radiology, pathology, and cardiology, the use of AI-based aproaches has expanded in ophthalmology due to widespread availbility of ophthalmic imaging. In particular, the AI subfields of mahine learning (ML) and deep learning (DL) are currently being sed in ophthalmology practices to revolutionize vision care. This aper aims to investigate the role of AI-based systems in performng medical work in each subfield of ophthalmology and evaluate he progress made in this area along with challenges.
