AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) gained renewed attention last year with the release of ChatGPT (OpenAI), an AI-powered language model that uses deep learning techniques to generate human-like text This revolutionary tool presents many opportunities as well as challenges in the field of scientific writing such as, for example, speeding up the writing and increasing the overall quality of texts (e.g. spelling, grammar, usage and style) Overall, these advantages are particularly useful for non-native English speakers, thus increasing inclusiveness However, concern has been expressed regarding the impact AI-generated texts on data reporting, plagiarism and fabrication ChatGPT has been even listed as a coauthor in some articles, a development with which many scientists and publishers disagree as AI-text generators do not meet the standard or criteria for authorship
