AID - 10.1016/j.jpra.2024.07.008 [doi]
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) has rapidly advanced across healthcare including plastic surgery. Among these innovations, text-to-image models represent a significant leap, promising to transform some aspects of clinical practice. Text-to-image models generally consist of two main components: a large language model (LLM) that converts the input text into a latent representation, and a generative image model that creates an image based on this representation.1 Due to their capability of producing increasingly realistic and detailed visuals, they have a vast potential as an innovative tool in plastic surgery.
