AB  - Atrial fibrillation (AF) is the most common sustained arrhythmia. Symptoms may include palpitations, dyspnea, limited exercise tolerance, and fatigue. However, AF is asymptomatic in 12%–25% of cases and remains undetected in 1.4% of patients aged >65 years.1,2 Early detection and adequate treatment of silent AF is essential, especially in patients who are at increased risk for stroke.
