TI  - Artificial Intelligence Electrocardiogram in Cardiac Intensive Care Unit Patients With Indeterminate Diastolic Function
FAU - Hillerson D
FAU - Harmon DM
FAU - Lee E
FAU - Oh JK
FAU - Jentzer JC.
DP  - 2026
AID - 10.1016/j.jacadv.2025.102406 [doi]
AB  - A bnormal diastolic function (DF) and elevated left ventricular filling pressures (FP) portend worse outcomes in patients with acute heart disease, including critically ill patients in the cardiac intensive care unit (CICU). 1,2 DF and FP are usually assessed by transthoracic echocardiogram (TTE), but the 2016 DF grading algorithms resulted in indeterminate DF in a substantial portion of patients. 3 The artificial intelligence–enabled electrocardiography (AIECG) for DF grade and FP, previously trained and tested in 274,710 patients, has been shown to provide risk stratification in CICU. 1,4 In 7,313 CICU patients where elevated FP was defined as a medial mitral E/e’ ratio > 15, AIECG showed an accuracy of 71.5% and a C-statistic of 0.68. 1 We sought to describe the epidemiology and outcomes of CICU patients with indeterminate DF by TTE and to determine whether AIECG DF grading can provide risk stratification in this population that was excluded from the AIECG derivation cohort. We hypothesized that mortality would differ by AIECG DF grade in CICU patients with indeterminate DF by TTE.
