AB  - Population-based breast cancer screening using mammography is currently performed worldwide [1].Considerable debate continues over the benefits and harms of mammography screening, including false-positive recalls, missed cancers in dense breasts, and cost-effectiveness in resource-limited areas [2].As part of efforts to address these limitations, artificial intelligence (AI) for mammography has been developed and validated and is now commercially available for clinical use.Prospective trials are currently underway in order to demonstrate the clinical feasibility of AI for mammography [3][4][5].
