AB  - Dear Editor, Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming the world we live in. The recent advances in AI and the use of ChatGPT (openAI, San Francisco, CA, USA) are revolutionizing industries ranging from finance to transportation system to healthcare system. AI is providing solutions to some of the most complex challenges faced by the healthcare industry, and public health is one area that has benefited significantly from AI. In a recently published correspondence, Situmorang asked an important question in the age of AI: Is AI a challenge or an opportunity? Situmorang then presented some insight that AI can provide for public health. He cited said that metaverse can become a ‘new place for everyone who can relish the online mental health meetings with a new atmosphere and sensation, especially in the post-COVID-19 era’.1 However, Corpuz responded to Situmorang saying that it is not clear which advantages the metaverse would have in treating mental health concerns with respect to the author’s proposal.2
