AB  - The Sociedad Española de Retina y Vítreo (Spanish Retina and Vitreous Society, SERV) was founded in 1993 and has 830 members today.SERV is a scientific entity whose main objective is to promote visual health and combat retinal diseases through research, innovation, training, and dissemination.These are the four pillars that support SERV's activity, with a global and collaborative perspective with other Spanish and international scientific societies.SERV congresses and sessions have so far been attended by 20,000 specialists and 600 Spanish and international speakers.It celebrated its 25th anniversary this year in 2022, demonstrating its firm commitment to excellence and the highest scientific quality.The Society complements these sessions annually by providing unique training opportunities in vitreous-retinal surgery and related areas through fellowships of varying lengths that include young ophthalmologists and researchers.The Society promotes monographs, manuals, and clinical practice guidelines, in which recommendations based on innovation and scientific evidence are established to support specialists in their daily decision making on the most appropriate medical care for each situation.
