AB  - Kidney stone analysis is a manual process, requiring trained personnel for assessment of stone chemical composition from absorbance spectra. Recently, we developed an artificial intelligence (AI)-based algorithm for quantitative determination of kidney stone composition from spectra that can also be utilized to check for manual spectral interpretation and transcription errors (1). Process errors are a persistent problem, the frequency of which can be described in defects per million (DPM), and/or by using sigma metrics (2). Manual processes in the clinical laboratory generally are believed to be associated with error rates of 2% to 4%, which corresponds to approximately 3.5 sigma (22 750 DPM) (3). Manual secondary review of manual processes is widely utilized to reduce/eliminate manual errors, and indeed is often required by regulation (College of American Pathologists 10/24/2022 General Laboratory Accreditation Checklist). However, the true efficacy of manual secondary review is difficult to assess and is not well characterized (4).
