AB  - BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES: The potential of artificial intelligence in medical practice is increasingly being investigated. This study aimed to examine OpenAI's ChatGPT in answering medical multiple choice questions (MCQ) in an Australian context. METHOD: We provided MCQs from the Australian Medical Council's (AMC) medical licencing practice examination to ChatGPT. The chatbot's responses were graded using AMC's online portal. This experiment was repeated twice. RESULTS: ChatGPT was moderately accurate in answering the questions, achieving a score of 29/50. It was able to generate answer explanations to most questions (45/50). The chatbot was moderately consistent, providing the same overall answer to 40 of the 50 questions between trial runs. DISCUSSION: The moderate accuracy of ChatGPT demonstrates potential risks for both patients and physicians using this tool. Further research is required to create more accurate models and to critically appraise such models.
