AB  - The rise of artificial intelligence (AI) in orthopaedic peer review brings a mix of exciting possibilities and serious concerns. On one hand, AI tools can streamline the manuscript evaluation process, making it quicker and more efficient. On the other hand, we must navigate significant risks that could compromise the integrity of reviews, such as confidentiality breaches and AI's potential to amplify existing biases. This editorial explores how AI affects the core responsibilities of peer reviewers, highlighting the vital importance of human oversight, transparency, and adaptability to ensure that our commitment to high-quality, rigorous orthopaedic research remains intact.
