AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) solutions are being adopted across the globe, including the Global South, to address health needs and strengthen health systems. The rapid adoption of AI solutions provides tremendous potential to redress health inequities and strengthen health systems. It also entails substantial risks of deepening inequities, creating new forms of exclusion and weakening fragile health systems. Drawing on field-based case studies and interdisciplinary consultations, this paper presents an emergent research landscape that prioritizes health equity, gender equality, ethical safeguards, inclusive governance and Global South leadership. Three entry points for implementation research are proposed, which are situated within five cross-cutting prerequisites.
