AB  - Dear Editor, In recent years, many individuals have turned to the Internet for health-related information, a phenomenon commonly referred to as "Dr. Google". While accessible, this practice often exposes users to unverified content, potentially leading to confusion and anxiety. With the rise of artificial intelligence (AI), the landscape is shifting: tools like ChatGPT offer structured, conversational responses. But how reliable are these answers, especially in the medical field? [...].
